\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces PCA on posterior mean peak ages by metric; four representative players are labelled per quadrant. The horizontal axis (PC1) captures overall peak timing --- all metric loadings share the same sign, so players toward the right peak later across the board (e.g.\ Nash, Stockton) and those toward the left peak earlier (e.g.\ Jonny Flynn, O.J.\ Mayo). The vertical axis (PC2) is a contrast in \emph  {relative} timing: players near the top have their defense and rebounding peak later (largely interior bigs, e.g.\ Gobert, Mutombo), while those near the bottom have their scoring and usage peak later (largely lead guards, e.g.\ Ginobili, Hornacek).\relax }}{14}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:metric_loadings}{{4}{14}{PCA on posterior mean peak ages by metric; four representative players are labelled per quadrant. The horizontal axis (PC1) captures overall peak timing --- all metric loadings share the same sign, so players toward the right peak later across the board (e.g.\ Nash, Stockton) and those toward the left peak earlier (e.g.\ Jonny Flynn, O.J.\ Mayo). The vertical axis (PC2) is a contrast in \emph {relative} timing: players near the top have their defense and rebounding peak later (largely interior bigs, e.g.\ Gobert, Mutombo), while those near the bottom have their scoring and usage peak later (largely lead guards, e.g.\ Ginobili, Hornacek).\relax }{figure.caption.6}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Posterior estimates of peak age by metric (left) and the first two PCA loadings of the peak-age matrix (right). Athleticism metrics (green) peak earlier; skill metrics (red) peak later; the ``both'' group (blue) blends the two. The analogous peak-value decomposition is provided in Appendix~\ref  {fig:peaks_vals}.\relax }}{15}{figure.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:peaks}{{5}{15}{Posterior estimates of peak age by metric (left) and the first two PCA loadings of the peak-age matrix (right). Athleticism metrics (green) peak earlier; skill metrics (red) peak later; the ``both'' group (blue) blends the two. The analogous peak-value decomposition is provided in Appendix~\ref {fig:peaks_vals}.\relax }{figure.caption.7}{}}
